{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "4: Telemetry archiving",
  "description": "End-to-end: the single-writer background sweep that copies new Copilot spans into a durable local archive before Copilot rotates them away, then prunes to the retention window. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "nextTour": "5: Workflow deviation markers",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Schedule the sweep",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 92,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-25.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `Sweep timer → CopilotArchiver: start() / tick()`**\n\n`CopilotArchiver.start` schedules a periodic `tick`. Copilot rotates its telemetry databases and prunes old rows, so the archiver's job is to copy new spans into a durable local archive before they vanish."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Elect a single writer",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 125,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-26.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotArchiver → WriterLease: tryAcquire() elect writer`**\n\nEach tick first calls `lease.tryAcquire()`. A `WriterLease` elects ONE writer across all open VS Code windows, so several windows never archive the same spans concurrently."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — Writer or reader",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 127,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-27.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `WriterLease → CopilotArchiver: writer or reader`**\n\nIf another window holds the lease, this instance is a pure reader — it drops its store and returns. Only the elected writer falls through to sweep."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Open the archive store",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 132,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-28.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotArchiver → Archive DB: open IngestStore(archive)`**\n\nThe writer lazily opens the archive database (`new IngestStore(archiveDbPath)`) — the append-only local store that outlives Copilot's own rotation."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Snapshot each source",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 172,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-29.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotArchiver → readonly snapshot: snapshot each Copilot source`**\n\nFor every Copilot source (never the archive itself), `sweepOnce` takes a read-only snapshot via `snapshotFactory` — the same WAL-replaying copy the views use, so archiving never mutates or races Copilot's live DB."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Read only new spans",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 181,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-30.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `readonly snapshot → CopilotArchiver: new spans above watermark`**\n\nUsing the per-source watermark, `readSpansSince(reader, since)` reads only spans newer than the last sweep — incremental, so a large DB is never re-copied every tick."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — Append and advance the watermark",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 183,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-31.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotArchiver → Archive DB: write new spans`**\n\nNew spans are appended with `store.writeSpans(rows)`, and the watermark advances (minus a small grace) so the next sweep resumes exactly where this one stopped."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 8 — Prune to retention",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/otel/copilotArchiver.ts",
      "line": 143,
      "description": "![4: Telemetry archiving](.tours/diagrams/d-32.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 8 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotArchiver → Archive DB: prune(retention)`**\n\nAfter sweeping, `store.prune(retentionMs, now)` drops spans older than the retention window. Pruned rows sit below the watermark, so pruning never triggers a re-ingest loop."
    }
  ]
}
